+**Branch**: `S007-review-state` | **Date**: 2026-08-10 | **Spec**: `spec.md`
+
+## Summary
+
+Implement the review state as small, pure array transformations in `web/app.js`, then render those transitions through native controls in `web/index.html`. The repository has no package manifest, framework, project design system, or existing test harness, so Node's built-in test runner is the smallest evidence-producing choice.
+
+## Technical Approach
+
+State is an array of item objects. Initialization copies each input item, normalizes it to `{ status: 'pending', selected: false }`, and rejects duplicate `id` values. Toggle and approval return the original state reference for inert operations; otherwise they return newly mapped item objects. Browser boot uses an internal state variable and event handlers, while the same three pure functions are exposed with `module.exports` when CommonJS is available.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- Requires: Node.js only for the local test runner.
+- Provides: deterministic, immutable review-state transitions and accessible review controls.
+
+## Testing Strategy
+
+- Unit tests: initialization, duplicate IDs, toggling, unknown IDs, approval, empty approval, and input immutability.
+- Browser-source checks: source-level assertions for CommonJS exports and accessibility attributes, plus manual inspection of the rendered controls where a browser is available.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: JavaScript (Node v24 available locally)
+**Primary Dependencies**: None
+**Storage**: N/A
+**Testing**: `node --test`
+**Target Platform**: Browser with CommonJS-compatible Node test execution
+**Project Type**: Static web page
+**Performance Goals**: Linear transitions over the supplied review items
+**Constraints**: No input mutation; no auto-confirmation; no external dependencies
+
+## Architecture Decision Gate
+
+This is a single-module change with no external service, persistence, or new architectural pattern. Keeping state transitions and browser wiring in `web/app.js` is the simplest adequate design.
+
+## Project Structure
+
+```
+web/
+├── app.js          # pure transitions, browser renderer, CommonJS exports
+├── app.test.js     # Node built-in unit tests
+└── index.html      # review surface and local styling
+```
