-# S007 Review selection state
+# Story: Review selection state
 
-Implement `initialState(items)`, `toggleSelection(state, id)`, and `approveSelected(state)` in `web/app.js` without mutating inputs.
+**Story ID**: `S007-review-state` · **Qualified**: `E001-capture-review/S007`
+**Status**: Specified
+**Input**: Give a reviewer clear, reversible selection and approval controls without mutating state.
 
-- Initial items are pending and unselected.
-- Toggle changes selection only for the matching id; unknown ids leave state unchanged.
-- Approval confirms only selected items, leaves others pending, and clears all selection. With no selection it leaves state unchanged.
-- Duplicate item ids are invalid.
-- Render buttons with truthful aria-pressed state and keep Approve disabled until at least one item is selected. Nothing is auto-confirmed.
-- Export the three functions with CommonJS while keeping browser use possible.
+## Purpose
+
+A reviewer needs to choose pending items deliberately and approve only that chosen set. The review surface must make selection state truthful to assistive technology and must never confirm an item without an explicit selection.
+
+## 1. Experience
+
+### 1a. JTBD Context
+
+When reviewing a set of pending items, the reviewer wants to select the items that are ready, so that approval is deliberate and the remaining work stays visible.
+
+### 1b. Primary User Story
+
+As a reviewer, I want to select pending items and approve the selection so that only the items I explicitly chose become confirmed.
+
+### 1c. Felt Quality
+
+| Surface | Entry emotional state | Target felt outcome | Banned feelings |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Review list | Careful and decisive | In control of exactly what will be approved | Surprise, ambiguity, accidental confirmation |
+
+## 2. Acceptance LARP
+
+#### Scenario: Select and approve a subset
+- **GIVEN** a review state with two pending, unselected items
+- **WHEN** the reviewer selects one item and activates Approve
+- **THEN** only that item is confirmed, all items are unselected, and the other item remains pending
+
+#### Scenario: Empty approval is inert
+- **GIVEN** a review state with no selected items
+- **WHEN** approval is requested
+- **THEN** the state is unchanged and the Approve control is disabled in the rendered UI
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown selection is inert
+- **GIVEN** a review state with known item IDs
+- **WHEN** selection is toggled for an unknown ID
+- **THEN** the state is unchanged
+
+## 3. Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: `initialState(items)` SHALL return a new pending, unselected state for every supplied item and SHALL reject duplicate item IDs.
+- **FR-002**: `toggleSelection(state, id)` SHALL toggle only the matching item and SHALL leave the state unchanged for an unknown ID.
+- **FR-003**: `approveSelected(state)` SHALL confirm only selected items, clear all selection, and SHALL leave an empty selection unchanged.
+- **FR-004**: The rendered item controls SHALL expose truthful `aria-pressed` values.
+- **FR-005**: The rendered Approve control SHALL remain disabled until one or more items are selected; rendering SHALL not auto-confirm any item.
+- **FR-006**: The three state-transition functions SHALL be available through CommonJS exports without breaking browser execution.
+
+## 4. Adversarial Cases
+
+| Condition | Must NOT happen | Probe |
+|---|---|---|
+| Duplicate IDs | Ambiguous selection | Assert that initialization throws |
+| Unknown ID | Existing item changes | Compare returned state identity and contents |
+| Empty selection | Any item is confirmed | Compare returned state identity and contents |
+| Rendered controls | Accessibility state drifts from state | Inspect `aria-pressed` and `disabled` after clicks |
+
+## 5. Non-Functional Requirements
+
+- Accessibility: native buttons, visible focus, truthful `aria-pressed`, and a disabled native approval button.
+- Data safety: all transitions are immutable; inputs and prior states are never changed.
+
+## Story Lifecycle State Tracking
+
+- [x] **Specified** - requirements completed
+- [x] **Planned** - technical approach completed
