+# UI Specification: Review selection controls
+
+**Story**: S007-review-state  
+**Epic**: E001-capture-review  
+**Project**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-10
+
+## Design Context Sources
+
+No project design system, UX strategy, wireframes, recipe, or primitive registry exists in this workspace. This specification therefore applies the repository evidence and the visual-quality baseline: clear hierarchy, purposeful spacing, visible focus, subtle surface depth, and native controls.
+
+## PROFILE Surface Impact
+
+- [x] No — the local review page is not a declared public profile surface.
+
+## Visual Assets Requirements
+
+- [x] No — this story needs no visual assets.
+
+## Component Overview
+
+**Component**: Review selection list  
+**Type**: Modified static page plus browser renderer  
+**Affects**: `web/index.html` and `web/app.js`
+
+## Component Anatomy
+
+```
+Review panel
+├── heading and supporting instruction
+├── pending item toggle buttons (one per item)
+└── Approve selected button
+```
+
+## States & Behavior
+
+| State | Item control | Approval control |
+|---|---|---|
+| Pending / unselected | neutral surface, `aria-pressed="false"` | disabled |
+| Pending / selected | raised accent surface, `aria-pressed="true"` | enabled |
+| Confirmed | muted confirmed label and non-selected state | disabled unless another pending item is selected |
+
+- Clicking an item uses its native button behavior; keyboard Enter and Space work without custom handlers.
+- Focus uses a custom high-contrast outline.
+- Hover and active styles provide a light lift and press response; reduced-motion users receive no transition.
+- Approval has no loading state because it is a synchronous local state transition.
+
+## Density & Responsive Behavior
+
+- One panel, one job, one primary action: approve the selected items.
+- At all widths the list is one column; the panel stays fluid with a readable maximum width.
+- Touch targets are at least 44px high.
+
+## Accessibility Requirements
+
+- Item controls are native `button` elements with `aria-pressed` derived from current state.
+- The approval control is a native disabled button until a selection exists.
+- Focus order follows the visual order.
+- A status region announces the count of selected items.
+
+## Implementation Guide
+
+- Render each item as a button with `data-id` and `aria-pressed`.
+- Keep browser event wiring separate from pure transitions inside the same module.
+- Use CSS custom properties local to `index.html`; no project tokens are available.
+
+## Testing Checklist
+
+- [ ] Selected and unselected states reflect state in `aria-pressed`.
+- [ ] Approval is disabled when no selection exists.
+- [ ] Keyboard activation works through native buttons.
+- [ ] Focus and reduced-motion styles are present.
+
